Apple has updated the design of the virtual Apple TV Remote for the iOS 27 Release Candidate, which was released yesterday, and there are two new features that have been added to the iPhone app's interface.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/Apple-TV-Remote-Icon.jpeg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1052069" /><br/>
First up, Apple has added a new button to the top-right corner of the Remote UI with a glyph showing four squares. Pressing the button pops out an app menu similar to the Apple TV home screen that allows you to quickly select an app and launch it.<br/>
<br/>
Second, you can now drag down from the top of the virtual trackpad with your finger to reveal the Apple TV's top shelf carousel, where shows in your watch list are displayed, along with shows that you've started so that you can continue watching.<br/>
<br/>
The two new features, hidden behind feature flags, were discovered by <em>MacRumors</em> and later <a href="https://x.com/itspdfu/status/2097817121321308547?s=20">demonstrated on X (Twitter)</a> by code sleuth "pdfu."<br/>
<br/>
